acceptance_criteria: "Preserve complete Unicode code points within the existing section size and ellipsis policy; cover ordinary and compact boundaries, short Unicode and long ASCII controls through source and built/packed public exports; behavioural revert fails; npm and Bun release checks pass unchanged."
resolution: Implemented and merged in #114 (3b25240).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #114 as 3b25240; checks successful at head 4663dc6: CodeQL, codeql, test (22.18.0), test (26), windows-acceptance-launcher."
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T12:45:28.080Z",codex-sol,"Reproduced the exact issue ES module on Node 24.19.0 after installing pm-slack-standup@2026.10.9 and @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.12 from the official registry with lifecycle scripts disabled in a disposable project. Input well formed: true; output well formed: false; output length: 3000; tail includes an unpaired high surrogate followed by the ellipsis. Short Unicode and long ASCII controls passed before the final assertion failed (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T12:45:29.818Z",codex-sol,"Imported only GitHub issue 113 using the already installed pm-github, --since 2026-10-12T08:44:48Z --atomic --gate after a dry run selected exactly one issue. Import receipt: 1 new, 0 updated, 0 skipped; privacy gate passed. UX gaps: import help has no issue-number or limit filter, so timestamp selection required verification. The gh issue view --comments command fails on deprecated projectCards; --json body,comments retrieves the complete issue. Plan: preserve the existing UTF-16 size budget, ellipsis and section count; stop clipping at a complete code point; exercise ordinary/compact Unicode boundaries via source, built and packed exports with real temporary tracker evidence, then prove a behavioural revert fails and run unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-12T12:53:07.611Z",codex-sol,"Implemented bounded code-point iteration in the shared buildBlockKit truncator, counting UTF-16 units and reserving one unit for the existing ellipsis. The 30 focused tests pass through pm test --run --progress: 14 source cases, 14 built-entry cases, real temporary tracker ordinary/compact exports, and an npm-installed tarball consumer running the same 14-case public-entry contract. PM test execution succeeded but automatic evidence recording is disabled by existing tracker policy, so this comment records the receipt explicitly. Tests cover short Unicode, long ASCII, non-BMP text before/across/after the cut and exactly/below the ceiling. Lint and zero-duplication checks pass."
  "2026-10-12T12:53:40.447Z",codex-sol,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only the shared truncate function with its baseline implementation, retained every new test, rebuilt dist with npm run build, then ran node --test --test-reporter=tap test/unicode-clipping.test.ts test/unicode-clipping-public.test.ts. Result: exit 1, 30 tests, 24 passed, 6 failed, 0 skipped/cancelled. Failures are ordinary/compact non-BMP across-cut cases in both source and built entries, the real tracker export integration, and the installed npm tarball consumer. The positive controls pass. Restored the fix and rebuilt dist before the release gates."
  "2026-10-12T13:02:25.445Z",codex-sol,"The initial isolated npm release check passed all 268 tests but failed function coverage because the new built-entry test statically loaded dist/index.js into the authored-source coverage process. Its source map remapped a second set of generated function counters onto index.ts (100% statements/branches/lines, 75.69% total functions). Moved built and packed public-entry contracts into separate real consumer processes with generated-artifact counters removed from their environments. The source regression remains instrumented; all four 100% thresholds and the complete authored-source inventory are unchanged. Repeating final-form regressions, behavioural revert and both release gates."
  "2026-10-12T13:03:38.698Z",codex-sol,"Final-form focused regression passes through pm test --run --progress: 17/17 outer tests plus 14/14 built public-entry and 14/14 installed npm tarball consumer cases. Repeated behavioural revert by replacing only truncate with the baseline and rebuilding first; node --test --test-reporter=tap test/unicode-clipping.test.ts fails with exit 1, 17 tests, 12 passed, 5 failed, 0 skipped/cancelled. Failures: source ordinary/compact non-BMP across-cut, built consumer, real tracker export, installed tarball consumer. Both public consumers fail on their ordinary/compact across-cut checks. Restored the fix and rebuilt successfully. Lint and zero duplication still pass."
  "2026-10-12T13:09:50.510Z",codex-sol,"The second isolated npm attempt passed all 255 tests but still reported duplicate generated function counters: Node child_process automatically restores an absent NODE_V8_COVERAGE key from the parent, as verified in the installed runtime implementation. The consumer environment now sets NODE_V8_COVERAGE to an empty value explicitly. A focused run with parent coverage enabled passes 17/17 and verifies zero generated public-entry scripts in authored-source counters. Repeated the behavioural revert on the final test implementation: 17 tests, 12 passed, 5 failed, no skips/cancellations; restored the fix and rebuilt. Typechecked tests, lint and zero duplication pass. No coverage threshold or authored-source exclusion changed."
  "2026-10-12T13:15:56.424Z",codex-sol,"Final npm release:check PASSED with a disposable HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: 255/255 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations; 100% lines/statements/branches/functions across all 11 authored source files, unchanged thresholds; 0 duplication; 89 documented declarations; production audit 0 vulnerabilities; canonical-reader acceptance passed; all 5 packed npm/Bun/current/minimum/global-host scenarios passed; changelog check, release-date and publish-attestation verification passed. The isolated bun run release:check is running against identical implementation and regression sources."
  "2026-10-12T13:19:43.196Z",codex-sol,"Final validation completed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS under disposable HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Each gate passes 255/255 tests (0 failures/skips/cancellations), 1/1 real canonical-reader acceptance and 5/5 packed npm/Bun/current/minimum/global-host scenarios. Every one of the 11 authored source files measures 100% lines/statements/branches/functions at unchanged thresholds; lint passes, duplication is 0%, 89 declarations are documented, production audit reports 0 vulnerabilities, and changelog/date/attestation checks pass. Final pm test --run --progress passes 17/17 focused tests plus two 14/14 public consumer contracts. Behavioural revert remains 12 passed/5 failed after rebuilding, with the fix restored. Code, built distribution and regression hashes match across both gates. Scope: complete code points within the existing UTF-16 budget and ellipsis policy, preserving section layout; verification uses local synthetic trackers and tarball consumers. pm-github UX gap: no number/limit selector, so a verified timestamp filter was necessary to import only issue 113. No pm CLI/SDK defect found. Releasing the claim and leaving the item in_progress for review."
