close_reason: "Delivered by #114 \"fix: preserve Unicode code points in Block Kit clipping\" (merged as 3b25240). Checks successful at the PR head 4663dc6: CodeQL, codeql, test (22.18.0), test (26), windows-acceptance-launcher."
body: "## Observed defect\n\n`buildBlockKit` cuts a valid supplementary Unicode character in half at its 3,000-unit section boundary, producing an unpaired high surrogate. This affects a long title or any generated section where an emoji/non-BMP character straddles the cut.\n\nReproduced on Node 24.19.0 against the **actual npm pm-slack-standup@2026.10.9 distribution** and independently against source commit **864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df**. npm `gitHead` matches that commit; the downloaded tarball's SHA-512 matched registry integrity:\n`sha512-X+zcKTFgspsxQAVOfSKWBrKy5I5UOFeFwQLwig/ekiN6BHOthC6C4U8XE6Sb0wXd20ccV+7QMef+ZlfCLDHYLA==`.\n\n[Source truncator](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/index.ts#L1701-L1744)\n\n## Sanitized reproduction\n\nIn a disposable directory, install `pm-slack-standup@2026.10.9` and `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.12` from the official npm registry with lifecycle scripts disabled, then run this as an ES module:\n\n```js\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { buildBlockKit } from \"pm-slack-standup\";\n\nconst opts = {\n  format: \"blockkit\", includeDone: true, groupBy: \"status\",\n  sections: [\"in_progress\"], mentionMap: {}, splitYesterday: false,\n  sectionLabels: {}, upNextCount: Infinity\n};\nfunction render(title) {\n  const data = {\n    wip: [{ id: \"pm-emoji\", title, status: \"in_progress\" }],\n    blocked: [], done: [], upNext: [], total: 1\n  };\n  return buildBlockKit(data, opts).blocks\n    .find(block => block.type === \"section\").text.text;\n}\nconst title = \"a\".repeat(2975) + \"😀\" + \"b\".repeat(100);\nconst output = render(title);\nconsole.log({\n  inputWellFormed: title.isWellFormed(),\n  outputWellFormed: output.isWellFormed(),\n  length: output.length,\n  tail: JSON.stringify(output.slice(-8))\n});\nassert.equal(render(\"Short 😀 title\").isWellFormed(), true);\nassert.equal(render(\"a\".repeat(3100)).isWellFormed(), true);\nassert.equal(render(\"a\".repeat(3100)).length, 3000);\nassert.equal(output.isWellFormed(), true); // Fails today\n```\n\nActual: input is well formed; output is not; length is 3000; tail contains `aaaaaa\\ud83d…`.\nExpected: clipping retains complete Unicode code points and stays within the existing size budget.\n\n## Impact and limits\n\nThe renderer itself demonstrably corrupts valid Unicode before delivery. This may produce replacement characters or downstream interoperability problems. No Slack request was sent, and this report does **not** claim a verified Slack API rejection.\n\nShort Unicode titles and long ASCII sections pass. The existing code-point-aware truncator in [pm-slack](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/blob/389ae059a6beea07e2d08e2daa3d97d9066102b5/index.ts#L1018-L1044) also preserves well-formedness for the equivalent boundary case.\n\n## Ownership and prior decisions\n\nChecked all 91 canonical PM item documents at the pinned tree, plus all-state GitHub issue/PR searches for surrogate, Unicode and truncation. No existing owner describes this defect.\n\nThe closed [Block Kit schema decision pm-slack-standup-rpty](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/.agents/pm/decisions/pm-slack-standup-rpty.toon) intentionally keeps one bounded section per bucket. Preserve that behavior. The closed [formatter test task pm-slack-standup-uf4j](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/.agents/pm/tasks/pm-slack-standup-uf4j.toon) covered validity/truncation but does not establish this Unicode boundary invariant.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Clip only at a complete code-point boundary while retaining the current length ceiling and ellipsis policy\n- Cover both ordinary and compact section rendering with non-BMP text at, before and after the clipping boundary\n- Retain the short-Unicode and long-ASCII positive controls\n- Run the regression against the built/packed public entry as well as source; do not require a Slack credential or live post"
